 have that  de-escalation as well  and so for me i went back and i had the  opportunity uh to finish playing  football  and so again it went from like a  semi-combative type environment to  war back into that semi-combative  environment and then back to kind of  being a normal person that wasn't  playing  a competitive sport and so i always  credit  uh that transition there was no master  plan i didn't understand that that's  what was happening but in hindsight i  think that really helped me kind of  transition  back was uh you know they kind of took  the guns away but there was still the  uniform there was still that  testosterone-driven combative  type environment um and so i think a lot  about like  uh everything is relative right of like  yeah sure i went back  into kind of the normal world it's just  the environment i went into  was probably much more advantageous for  me than if i had just been a  21 year old kid who just got thrown back  into the real world  um you know i was already doing some  pretty stupid stuff in terms of you know  bought a motorcycle and go 100 miles an  hour and say well you know find a diet  war like you know whatever here  but uh having that transition i think  was really helpful  um and then for 2020 uh  i think that really the thing that um  kind of just got hammered home is like  nobody knows the future  like literally nobody knows the future  and it seems like every time  uh something crazy happened it'd be like  oh man how much crazier could it get  and then like literally like within 12  hours like something even crazier would  happen  um and so if you even look at like 20 21  i think a lot of people have this like  psychological  okay we made it through 2020 like take a  deep breath like it's over  and there was definitely this like  turning of the page and then like we're  six seven days into 2021 now we're like  wait a minute is 2021 gonna be even  wilder than last year  um and so it's just like you can't  control the stuff and a lot of what you  started off the conversation around just  like your ability to adapt to  uh the things that happen are really  important um  and uh i'll leave you with this one  controversial topic that i've talked  about  online uh ad nauseam and people hate  when i say this  uh but i say it because it's true is i  don't believe in luck  and when i say that people are like what  do you mean you don't believe in luck  and i say well  we confuse the mathematical concept of  randomness with the psychological  concept of luck and i always use the  extreme example of like  if somebody goes to war and they lose  their arm and leg  a lot of people be like man that was  really unlucky but if you talk to that  person they'll say  no i'm lucky like i'm alive and so luck  is really  a mental perspective on an event that  happened  right the reason why that person lost  their arm and leg  there's a sense of randomness right are  they the one who sat in that seat versus  somebody else are they the one that was  in that vehicle versus a different  vehicle right  um and so i think that when you start to  really unpack kind of the mathematical  concept from the psychological concept  you realize and there's studies that  show like you actually can change your  luck  simply by changing the way you view the  events that happen  sounds really stupid sounds like oh of  course then why aren't we all lucky all  the time  but i do think that there's you know a  lot of truth in that and so it kind of  just puts you back in the control seat a  little bit and say look you can't  predict the future you can't control the  things that  uh happen but you can control how you  respond to them and i think that that's  kind of  you know really what it sounds like you  spend most of your day trying to hammer  home to a lot of these athletes and  clients like  exactly like it couldn't i couldn't even  say it better myself i think  you know just to like round all that out  that mental toughness  it doesn't make you invincible it makes  you adaptable it makes you  it allows you to see things from  different perspectives  when you get dealt a crappy hand of  cards you have the opportunity to see it  one way or the other way  when my parents got divorced i could  have you know when i look back i  you could i could tell you how horrible  it was and all the bad things but i can  also tell you all the good things that  came from it  you know that every every bad moment we  can learn something from and i think all  that comes down to is this power of  choice that we have  and that's what i think mental toughness  provides is it provides us more choices  and more  uh choices to adapt versus just to i  guess  fall victim to some of the default  settings absolutely  makes a ton of sense um where can we  send people to find you on the internet  i know you've been creating a ton of  content  uh you've got a newsletter that's coming  out uh where do we want to send them  to uh to find you and learn more about  some of the work that you're doing  so you can find me on instagram and when  i got married last year i changed my  name from a barca which was my maiden  name  to now johnson turns out there's a lot  of lauren nicole johnson's in this world  so  all my handles are different um i wish  they weren't but  my instagram handle pay attention is  laura nicole johnson  uh twitter is at underscore lauren  johnson  underscore and you can find me on  linkedin and i just  um shout out to ari lewis for uh  inspiring me to get a tick tock  um it's at lauren johnson with an  extra n at the end i believe okay good  luck okay i got it  uh when you create content what platform  do you think first to post it is it  instagram  twitter twitter yeah i twitter and  linkedin actually  those are my those are my top two and  then i usually go instagram and then  and then tick talk and and like you said  i am  in the in the midst of creating a  newsletter and so if you want to sign up  for that ahead of  time you can at any of my links on my  twitter and my instagram and my link  tree  awesome all right well listen i really  really appreciate this lauren i think  people are going to learn a ton from it  so  thanks so much for doing a lot to do to  get in the future yeah i'd love that  thanks for having me
 

